{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":496997,"name":"Franco Tomás García","username":"francotgs","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/ecb155/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:46:47.968Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter Grok Bot is closed, launching it again from the Start menu, a shortcut, or the executable can create background Electron processes but no visible application window. Restarting Windows temporarily recovers it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe failure was isolated to %APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\window-state.json. The file contained a window rectangle far outside the only connected display, with width and height both equal to zero. On the failing launch, the Electron main process remained responsive but had MainWindowHandle = 0.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoving only window-state.json aside restored the visible window immediately. Bots, conversations, credentials, and Agent Computer data were not changed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRun Grok Bot 0.57.1 on Windows with display scaling set to 150%.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUse the app normally with its window maximized.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClose the Grok Bot window using the title-bar close control.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLaunch Grok Bot again from Start, a shortcut, or %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Grok Bot\\Grok Bot.exe.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve that the Electron process tree starts, but no Grok Bot window becomes visible.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdditional launch attempts may create Crashpad reports and/or leave the process tree alive without a main window.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis occurred repeatedly after closing the desktop app. A Windows restart allowed one normal opening, after which closing and reopening could trigger it again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot should validate persisted window geometry and either restore the last valid visible bounds or use default centered bounds. Closing and reopening the app should never require restarting Windows or manually resetting application state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot:\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 0.57.1\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nArchitecture: Windows x64\u003cbr\u003e\nElectron: 42.1.0\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: Windows Enterprise 25H2, build 26200.9448, x64\u003cbr\u003e\nDisplay: one primary display, 1280x800 (working area 1280x752)\u003cbr\u003e\nDisplay scaling: 150% (AppliedDPI = 144)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExact persisted state captured during the failure:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"json\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-json\"\u003e{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"normalBounds\": {\n    \"x\": -21326,\n    \"y\": -21333,\n    \"width\": 0,\n    \"height\": 0\n  },\n  \"isMaximized\": true\n}\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt 150% scaling, those logical coordinates are approximately -31989, -32000 physical pixels, resembling Windows’ special minimized/off-screen coordinate. The zero size is invalid regardless of the source.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStructured log evidence (2026-09-21, America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires, UTC-03:00):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e10:08:50.897 — sand.desktop.startup, outcome=failed, phase=window, error_code=SAND-E0601, hw_accel=false\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e10:08:50.897 — sand.desktop.renderer_lifecycle, state=gone, reason=launch_failed, exit_code=21, error_code=SAND-E0605\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e10:08:50.898 — sand.desktop.unclean_exit, error_code=SAND-E0610\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe same sequence repeated at 10:08:54.218 and 10:09:58.123.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSix Crashpad dumps were created between 10:08:46 and 10:12:14. Windows Application Event Log had no matching Application Error entry.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003edesktop-status.json retained PID 20364 after that process no longer existed, though the stale PID alone did not prevent a new process tree from starting.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDirect verification:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWith the invalid file present, no processes existed before launch. Launching created the full Electron process tree, but the responsive main process had no title and MainWindowHandle = 0.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAfter moving only window-state.json to a backup, the same executable created a visible window titled Grok Bot with a non-zero native handle.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThis isolates the visible-launch failure to persisted desktop window state, rather than shortcut, authentication, Bot state, or Agent Computer state.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProposed fix:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eKeep lastKnownGoodNormalBounds and update it only while the window is normal and visible.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDo not persist geometry while minimized, destroyed, fullscreen, hidden, or transitioning during shutdown.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReject non-finite coordinates, non-positive or below-minimum sizes, and rectangles without meaningful overlap with any current display work area.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf bounds are invalid, ignore both the rectangle and isMaximized, then use normal default bounds.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClamp valid partially off-screen bounds to the selected display work area.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd regression tests for this exact state, high-DPI scaling, disconnected secondary displays, and close events while maximized/minimized.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe overlap check should require at least a small visible area (for example 100x40 pixels) on a current work area before restoring or persisting the rectangle.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnofficial Grok Bot 0.18 reconstruction with a similar defensive strategy (not the official source):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/AkiKurisu/grok-bot/tree/main/source/electron-main\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003egrok-bot/source/electron-main at main · AkiKurisu/grok-bot · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorkaround: fully terminate Grok Bot.exe, rename %APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\window-state.json, and relaunch. Resetting the entire user-data directory is unnecessary.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePossibly related but apparently separate process-cleanup report:\u003c/p\u003e\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"170121\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/i/82dd89/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-title__text-content\"\u003e\n      \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/new-report-windows-leftover-daemon-on-0-30-0/170121\"\u003eNew report, Windows, leftover daemon on 0.30.0\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/support/bug-report/6\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #652D90; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF; --parent-category-badge-color: #12A89D;\" data-parent-category-id=\"21\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square --has-parent\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003eBug Reports\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    \u003ca name=\"p-479391-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-479391-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nGrok Bot \n\u003ca name=\"p-479391-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-479391-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\nGrok Bot desktop on Windows loses the local-computer link after the app has been healthy. Same failure sequence as the macOS local-exec-daemon report. Still happening on 0.30.0 after \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/colin\"\u003e@Colin\u003c/a\u003e said 19 Aug a fix was ready for the next release. \nThe PC is reached through a detached local-exec daemon: \n%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Grok Bot\\Grok Bot.exe \n%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Grok Bot\\resources\\app.asar\\dist\\local-exec-daemon\\main.cjs …\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-496997-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-496997-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:48:44.206Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":13,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":66.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":172502,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen","display_username":"Franco Tomás García","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/new-report-windows-leftover-daemon-on-0-30-0/170121","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"New report, Windows, leftover daemon on 0.30.0","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/AkiKurisu/grok-bot/tree/main/source/electron-main","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"grok-bot/source/electron-main at main · AkiKurisu/grok-bot · GitHub","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139033,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen/172502/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":496998,"name":"Discourse AI Spam Scanner","username":"discourse_ai_spam","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/c68b51/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:46:58.196Z","cooked":"","post_number":2,"post_type":3,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:46:58.196Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":0.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":172502,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen","display_username":"Discourse AI Spam Scanner","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":-3,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"action_code":"visible.disabled","post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen/172502/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":497003,"name":"system","username":"system","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/system/{size}/99069_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:48:44.217Z","cooked":"","post_number":5,"post_type":3,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:48:44.217Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172502,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen","display_username":"system","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":-1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"action_code":"visible.enabled","post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen/172502/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":497327,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:52:30.722Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/francotgs\"\u003e@francotgs\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the detailed report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo separate things are going on here. The window-state.json you captured is real and I’ve flagged it to the team: the app is recording the position of a minimized window as if it were the normal one. On its own, though, that file is ignored on the next launch (the app falls back to its default window size), so it is not what stops the window from appearing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe launches that produce no window are the ones in your log with \u003ccode\u003eexit_code=21\u003c/code\u003e. That code means Windows refused to let the app start its sandboxed window process. Based on your report it sounds like the window is opening normally again!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHave you reproduced the issue since it happened the first time?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":11,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T18:52:47.939Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172502,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen/172502/11","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":498074,"name":"Franco Tomás García","username":"francotgs","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/ecb155/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-22T11:56:20.276Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey Colin, thanks for looking into this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes, I reproduced it again and isolated a consistent launcher-context difference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA normal mouse click on the original icon launches the correct signed executable from the regular desktop Explorer process, with no arguments. The main process starts Crashpad and several utility processes, but the window process dies almost immediately, no window is created, and all Grok Bot processes exit. A failed manual launch also created a new approximately 34.8 MB Crashpad dump.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not limited to reopening too quickly. Before the monitored test, Grok Bot had been closed for several minutes and process monitoring confirmed that no Grok Bot processes were running. The original icon still failed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI created a workaround that starts the exact same executable through a hidden, non-elevated PowerShell process. It also checks that no previous Grok Bot processes remain, but during the A/B comparison that condition was already satisfied immediately, so its success cannot be attributed to additional waiting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI manually tested repeated open/close cycles, including with the workaround pinned to the taskbar, and every launch succeeds. During the same Windows session, with no reboot or application-state change between tests, the original icon continues to fail.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe reproducible A/B result is therefore:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eExplorer.exe -\u0026gt; Grok Bot.exe\u003c/code\u003e: fails\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eExplorer.exe -\u0026gt; powershell.exe -\u0026gt; Grok Bot.exe\u003c/code\u003e: succeeds\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe window-state file was valid during these failures. This strongly suggests that the Windows launcher or inherited process/token context is relevant to the \u003ccode\u003eexit_code=21\u003c/code\u003e sandbox failure. Could the team capture the underlying Win32 error for \u003ccode\u003eSBOX_ERROR_SET_THREAD_TOKEN\u003c/code\u003e, or compare the renderer launch token when the parent is Explorer versus PowerShell?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can provide the Crashpad dumps privately if useful.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":12,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-22T11:56:20.276Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":11,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172502,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen","display_username":"Franco Tomás García","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139033,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen/172502/12","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":498502,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:50:51.681Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/francotgs\"\u003e@francotgs\u003c/a\u003e!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHave a look over here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"35\" data-topic=\"171690\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea3.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/48/90452_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-title__text-content\"\u003e\n      \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/when-we-open-the-cursor-it-crashes-the-application/171690/35\"\u003eWhen we open the cursor it crashes the application\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/support/bug-report/6\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #652D90; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF; --parent-category-badge-color: #12A89D;\" data-parent-category-id=\"21\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square --has-parent\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003eBug Reports\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    Hey all! \nIt looks like this might be an issue affecting more than just Cursor (and Grok Bot), but all applications which rely on Chromium sandbox tokens. \n\n\nKB5124008 seems to be where issues started, which may have been carried forward by KB5129195 / KB5129241. I have KB5129195 installed on my Windows device and do not experince the issue with crashing. \nUninstalling KB5124008 seems to resolve the issue on the affected device, although on managed devices that is probably easier said than done. …\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI think this issue is affecting more than just Cursor/Chromium, and ultimately has to do with some Windows security updates. I need to dig a bit more.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":19,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-22T19:50:51.681Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":172502,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/when-we-open-the-cursor-it-crashes-the-application/171690/35","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"When we open the cursor it crashes the application","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-57-1-on-windows-saves-a-0x0-off-screen-window-state-and-cannot-reopen/172502/19","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":498625,"name":"Franco Tomás García","username":"francotgs","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/ecb155/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-23T00:16:14.855Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/colin\"\u003e@Colin\u003c/a\u003e , thanks for looking into this!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI checked the Windows updates on my device: KB5124008 was installed on September 14 and KB5129241 on September 18. It’s running Windows 11 25H2, build 26200.9448; KB5129195 is not installed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat seems consistent with the Windows update connection you mentioned. The original Grok Bot launch still fails on my device with KB5129241 installed, though the alternative launcher is working well for me in the meantime.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks again for digging into it.\u003c/p